  "status": "authored 2026-10-08; offline checks only (tools/gym_arenas.py check). Nothing here has been built in a world or seen in a running game.",
  "name": "The Tracking Floor",
  "reading": "Koga's town is a fen-edge watch town whose trackers read the marsh for anyone passing unseen (docs/world-building/TOWN_CHARACTER.md gym5_town: mangrove, mud brick, packed mud, bamboo, dark oak; its signature dressing is a board of cast prints). The Reed House above is their watch house. Under it, below the marsh, is the range where the trackers learn to read: a low mud-brick floor in half-light, mangrove roots grown down through the roof, a trail of prints set into the floor, and woven reed screens that hide the far end. A player comes down the trackers' stair, a spiral round a mangrove post, into the south-east corner and walks west the length of a lane behind a screen, turns north, walks back east behind the next, and turns again: only under the third screen's end does the range open and the blind show, a raised hide at the far end with a plank roof and Koga half in shadow in it, three courses above the floor.",
  "leader": {
    "id": "kanto_koga",
    "seat": [
      4586,
      103,
      2461
    ],
    "seat_why": "in the deck of the blind (y103, floor y100 + 3), on the range's axis (x4586, the centre of the 34-wide floor), two in from the front of the hide. THE ONE SOURCE of Koga's seat once this record exists (tools/gym_arenas.py leader_seats): data/gym_buildings/gym5.json leader.spawner (4594, 131, 2487) is where the building puts the spawner the arena step then moves."
  },
