    "why": "Cobblemon Battle Positions (a Cobbleverse dependency, already installed): its search finds these from the challenger's feet and sends both Pokemon to them. The Pokemon blocks sit one under the floor's top course, so spawnHeightOffset 2.0 stands each Pokemon ON the floor; the trainer stand is under the deck one in front of the seat, behind the packed-mud face, so Koga steps to the front of the hide. Koga's Pokemon is 5.5 from the dais face (clear radius 3.13, Drapion's model sweep: 2.4 to spare); the two Pokemon are 5 apart (Drapion's hitbox is 2.02 wide); the challenger stands 3 behind their own."
